Flow: Payment

Chain:
  AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

Note — two separate relationships, do not conflate:

  Execution Chain (this file — what order to work in):
    AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

  Dependency Graph (see project/dependencies.sdd, and payment.sdd's own
  DependsOn/UsedBy — what depends on what):
    DB -> BE -> API -> (FE, MD) -> QA -> DO -> VR

  Mechanics (TransitionRules [T1]-[T10], DependencyRules, FailureRouting)
  for every stage below are defined once in @protocol/stages.sdd and MUST
  NOT be re-listed here (R2) — this file only instantiates them for
  Payment: what each stage actually needs/produces in this module, and
  which stages are conditional here.

Stages (prompt/new/15.md StageContract, Payment-instantiated):

  AN:
    input:      requirement, related_cases (@cases), existing_model (payment.sdd)
    output:     analysis, affected_parts, required_stages
    next:       AR
    fail:       AN

  AR:
    input:      analysis, DependsOn (Course, User), applicable_skills
    output:     architecture_decision
    next:       DB
    fail:       AR

  DB:
    optional
    condition:  database-impact = true
    # AI does not decide on its own to skip DB — this file declares the
    # condition explicitly (see prompt/new/9.md point 4).
    input:      data_requirements, existing @db model (escrow_transaction, ledger)
    output:     database_decision
    next:       BE
    skip:       BE
    fail:       DB

  BE:
    input:      architecture_decision, database_decision, backend_skills
    output:     backend_implementation, tests
    # backend_implementation here specifically means: PaymentService
    # (hold/release/refund escrow) — see @api -> Services.
    next:       API
    fail:       BE

  API:
    condition:  api-impact
    input:      backend_output
    output:     api_contract (@api)
    next:       FE
    skip:       FE
    fail:       BE   # per protocol/stages.sdd DefaultFailureRouting

  FE:
    input:      api_contract, frontend_skills
    output:     frontend_implementation, tests
    next:       MD
    fail:       FE

  MD:
    condition:  mobile-impact
    input:      api_contract, mobile_skills
    output:     mobile_implementation, tests
    next:       QA
    skip:       QA
    fail:       MD

  QA:
    input:      BE, API, FE, MD outputs, test_cases (@cases)
    output:     test_result, defects
    next:       DO
    fail:       responsible_stage   # e.g. a payment-state defect -> BE, a UI defect -> FE

  DO:
    condition:  infrastructure-impact
    input:      validated_application
    output:     deployment_result
    next:       VR
    skip:       VR
    fail:       DO

  VR:
    input:      completed_flow, validation_results
    output:     verification_result
    next:       DONE
    fail:       responsible_stage

Skills (third layer — which skill runs at each execution-chain stage):
  BE:  .sdd/backend/architecture, .sdd/backend/ddd, .sdd/backend/clean-code,
       .sdd/backend/security, .sdd/backend/testing
  FE:  .sdd/frontend/architecture, .sdd/frontend/components, .sdd/frontend/accessibility
  MD:  .sdd/mobile/architecture, .sdd/mobile/api, .sdd/mobile/testing
  QA:  .sdd/qa/bdd, .sdd/qa/integration, .sdd/qa/regression
  DO:  .sdd/devops/docker, .sdd/devops/ci-cd, .sdd/devops/observability

State (see @protocol/symbols.sdd for the full vocabulary):
  AN +, AR +, DB ?, BE ?, API ?, FE ?, MD ?, QA ?, DO ?, VR ?
